  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 259 PM EDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\n- Dry weather tonight and Tuesday\n\nHigh pressure will bring fair weather tonight through Tuesday as\nhigh pressure slips away to the southeast of the Great Lakes\nregion. A cooler night than normal for this time of year is\nexpected tonight with lows in the 50s. Highs on Tuesday will reach\nthe middle 80s in most locations. \n\n- Multiple chances for showers/storms Tues. night through Sat.\n\nA surface cold front will push into the area Tuesday night and\nwash out over Lower Michigan on Tuesday. The weak surface boundary\nwill be a impetus for showers and thunderstorms at times from\nTuesday night into Thursday. The pattern will be evolving into a\ntrough over the Great Lakes during this time. Embedded shortwaves\nwithin the flow will aid in precipitation production as well.\nWednesday through Thursday are the forecast periods where the best\nchances for rain look to occur. Highest chances for precipitation\noccur during this time frame 60-70 pct. \n\nDew points pool along the front rebounding back into the 60s. Most\nunstable CAPE values push into the 1000-2000 j/kg range. The\nprecipitation looks to be diurnally driven as is usually the case\nwith mid summer upper troughs. Cannot rule out some stronger\nstorms Wednesday afternoon into Wednesday night as the main\nshortwave moves through combined with 50+ knots in the mid levels\nat 500mb. At this point we are just in a general thunder outlook\nfrom the SPC. \n\nThe next time frame of concern is out Saturday night into Sunday\nwith the passage of another upper shortwave. Showers and storms\nare possible during this time as well. Surface dew points surge\ninto the 70s with the passage for a surface front. Only 20-30 pct\npops in the forecast at this point but this will be increased when\nmodel continuity increases. \n\n- Seasonable temperatures through the 7 day forecast\n\n850mb temperatures are in the middle to upper teens C which is\ntypical for mid summer. Mid to upper 80s highs are expected for\nthe most part through the period. Low temperatures will be\nseasonable as well in the mid to upper 60s.",
